From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll, ntlanman, shell32, mpr, explorer: a network place that cannot be reached says why, in Windows' words; saved and remembered credentials

A network place that could not be reached never said why. Every failure to
reach \\server\share was ERROR_BAD_DEV_TYPE (66, "The network resource type
is not correct"); File Explorer opened an empty folder for \\NOSUCHPC, asked
for a name and password for a misspelt share (\\server\NoShare) and then said
"can't find ... Check the spelling"; the password prompt had no "Remember my
credentials", and credentials saved for a server were never used when one of
its shares was reached again (a new sign-in asked again). As Windows does:

- ntdll: sg-netmountd's reason becomes the status: the computer is not there
  or does not answer STATUS_BAD_NETWORK_PATH (ERROR_BAD_NETPATH, 53), it has no
  such share STATUS_BAD_NETWORK_NAME (67, sg-session 0.1.0-306 answers ERR 2),
  it refuses the user STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED (5); ntlanman maps ERR 2 to
  ERROR_BAD_NET_NAME.
- shell32's Network folder: \\computer is looked up as a share is (its IPC$,
  through sg-netmountd's name lookup and SMB check) and fails with
  ERROR_BAD_NETPATH when nothing is there; a share's own error is returned;
  "Enter network credentials" comes only for a share that refuses the user,
  after the credentials saved for the computer, with "Remember my
  credentials" -- saved for the computer (a domain password credential, as
  Map Network Drive saves them) once the server took them.
- mpr: a connection made without a name or password that the server refuses
  is tried with the credentials Credential Manager keeps for the server, as
  Windows' redirector does.
- File Explorer: an address that cannot be reached shows "Network Error" --
  "File Explorer cannot access \\server\share", what to check, "See details"
  with the error code and its text, Diagnose (the network status in
  Settings) -- or "You do not have permission to access ..." for a refused
  share; "explorer \\server" does the same and opens no window (it opened
  This PC; a UNC folder is never handed to ShellExecute).

Gate: test/netreach-gate.sh (a stand-in sg-netmountd, test/netreach-netmountd.py,
in a private network and mount namespace with a /run of its own; probe
test/netreach-probe.c). Mutants SG_MUTANT_NET_ONE_STATUS, SG_MUTANT_NET_ANY_COMPUTER,
SG_MUTANT_NET_PROMPT_ALWAYS, SG_MUTANT_NET_NO_REMEMBER, SG_MUTANT_NO_SAVED_CRED_USE,
SG_MUTANT_NO_NETWORK_ERROR.
